# Tier: config -- the configure-option sweep.  test/config/option_sweep.sh
#
# Closes gap G14: 42 of 54 configure options were never built in CI, including
# --enable-o_direct, which is how defect P2 survived -- nothing ever compiled
# or ran that path.
#
# ONE OPTION AT A TIME (never combinatorially), and options that change RUNTIME
# behaviour additionally run test/config/config_smoke.c, because
# --enable-o_direct builds perfectly and fails at runtime: a build-only sweep
# would have reported it green.
#
# `complete` is the completeness gate itself, and it is MANDATORY and listed
# FIRST: every configure option must be in a sweep list or on the commented
# exclusion list, so adding an option forces a testing decision.  That is the
# same discipline this file applies to tests.  Without this entry a sweep could
# run every leg it knows about against a list that had silently lost half the
# options.
#
# The per-option legs are `optional` because the sweep is a NIGHTLY job that
# needs ~30 configure+build cycles (roughly 40 min on 12 jobs), not a per-PR
# gate -- but once the tier runs at all, check_manifest.sh reports each absent
# leg, and option_sweep.sh separately fails if the number of recorded legs does
# not match the number planned.  A leg that wrote no row did not run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
