# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tier: shape -- the SCALING-SHAPE gate.  test/bench/scale_shape_gate.sh
#
# Closes gaps G12 + G13.  libdb's TPROC-C throughput PEAKS AT 8 THREADS and
# falls to 32% of that peak by 96, while WiredTiger rises monotonically; all 34
# CI jobs run on a 2-4 vCPU ubuntu-latest runner that CANNOT produce the
# contention, and the one perf job is continue-on-error "informational only".
#
# The gate asserts SHAPE -- median tpm(t=32) >= median tpm(t=8) within a
# tolerance derived from the reps' own spread -- not an absolute number, because
# a shape comparison is between two measurements minutes apart on the same box
# and so survives a machine-class change that would invalidate a stored number.
#
# `selftest` is the TEETH entry and is MANDATORY: it feeds the same verdict code
# the measured libdb shape (must FAIL) and the measured WiredTiger shape (must
# PASS).  It needs no benchmark run and takes seconds, so it is the one entry
# that can be mandatory everywhere.  It has already earned its place -- it
# caught a ModuleNotFoundError in the gate that was exiting non-zero and being
# read as "correctly failed the descending series".
#
# `gate` is optional because it requires a 32+ core machine: the script REFUSES
# to emit a verdict below 32 cores (exit 3) rather than produce a number that
# describes the scheduler.  It runs in the nightly scale-shape workflow.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
shape	selftest
shape	gate	optional

